{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 100, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a skip_connect on edge 4 with a conv gave +3 to +8 points on all datasets, far more than any other edge-4 edit."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Upgrading edge 3 from avg_pool gained +4.35/+5.42/+6.13 when edge 4 was skip_connect versus about +1/+2/+4 with a conv on edge 4."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "With a weak skip on edge 2, replacing the edge 5 conv with avg_pool dropped -6.7/-11.9/-12.0 versus about -2/-3.5/-5.8 with a conv."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "An avg_pool on edge 2 made the edge 5 avg_pool edit much more damaging (-6.1/-12.7/-12.7) than a conv on edge 2."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Edge 2 to skip_connect cost -2.6/-7.1/-4.7 when edge 4 was already skip_connect, versus roughly -0.3/-1.3/-0.4 with a conv."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Edge 1 to skip_connect lost -4.3/-9.3/-10.7 when edge 5 was skip_connect versus -1.2/-2.6/-1.8 with a conv on edge 5."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing edge 0 when edge 1 is also none cuts the main path and cost -6.4/-13.6/-16.1, far worse than when edge 1 has an op."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Removing edge 5 hurts much less (-0.9/-2.3/-3.6) when edge 3 is a strong 3x3 conv providing a direct alternative path."}, {"edit_edge